"demo.snippet.coffeeOcrManual" = "📷 OCR Text Extraction [Confidence: 99.4% | Source Image: Roast_Level_Diagram.png]\n\n## Coffee Bean Roasting Stages & Flavor Evolution Curve\n\nCoffee beans undergo dehydration, First Crack, Maillard reaction, and Second Crack during roasting. Flavor profiles vary significantly across roast spectrums:\n\n| Roast Level | English Designation | Key Flavor Attributes | Acidity / Bitterness | Recommended Brewing |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Light Roast** | Light / Cinnamon | Floral, citrus, bright crisp acidity | High acidity, minimal bitterness | Pour-over, Syphon |\n| **Medium Roast** | Medium / City | Nutty, caramel, balanced chocolate | Balanced acidity & sweetness | Americano, SOE Espresso |\n| **Dark Roast** | Dark / French | Smoky, dark cocoa, rich body | Low acidity, pronounced bold bitter | Cold Drip, Milk Espresso |\n\n> 💡 **RAG Cross-reference**: When matching roast curves for bean procurement, cross-check against [[Roasting Factory & Origin Sourcing]] and the Dial-in table in [[Coffee Shop Daily Operations Manual]].";

"demo.snippet.coffeeVoiceProcure" = "🎙️ Voice-to-Text Transcript [Recording Duration: 03:45 | Accuracy Confidence: 98.6%]\n\n## 1. Core Commercial Espresso & Grinder Procurement List\n\n- **Espresso Machine**: La Marzocco Linea PB 2-Group Espresso Machine (with dual PID temp control and auto-backflush group heads). Budget capped at ¥85,000.\n- **Espresso Grinders**: Mahlkönig E65S GBW (Grind-by-Weight with millisecond electronic dosing). Quantity: 2 units, Budget ¥38,000.\n- **Single-Origin Grinder**: EK43S All-around Commercial Grinder (White Limited Edition) for SOE beans, Budget ¥22,000.\n\n## 2. Water Filtration & Conditioning System\n\n- **Whole-Store Filtration**: Commercial BWT dual soft-water filter system maintaining TDS between 75-120 ppm to prevent boiler scaling.\n\n## 3. Auxiliary Equipment & Bar Tools\n\n1. Smart dual-door undercounter refrigerated workbench (1.8m) x2 units.\n2. Puqpress Q3 Gen 5 auto tamper, Acaia Pearl timer scales x3 sets.\n3. Budget Summary: Hardware total ~¥165,000. 40% initial payment with 12 monthly installments. See [[Coffee Bean Supply Chain Cost Breakdown]].";

"demo.snippet.luckin" = "# 📊 China Coffee Chain Market: Luckin vs. Starbucks Business Model Analysis\n\n> This report delivers an in-depth evaluation of single-store unit economics, cost structures, and supply chain strategies for two leading coffee giants to support cafe site selection.\n\n## 1. Core Strategy & Positioning Comparison\n\n- **Starbucks**: Focuses on the \"Third Space\" social experience. Average store footprint: 150-250 ㎡ with high lease costs, relying on premium ticket sizes (¥35-45).\n- **Luckin Coffee**: Focuses on \"Pick-up outlets\" and digital app ordering. Average store footprint: 20-50 ㎡ with high sales density and viral product hit rates (e.g., Coconut Latte).\n\n## 2. Unit Economics & Cost Structure Matrix\n\n| Cost Structure Ratio | Starbucks Flagship | Luckin Grab-and-Go | Independent Cafe (Ref) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Cost of Goods Sold (COGS)** | 28% - 32% | 35% - 38% | 30% - 35% |\n| **Rent & Property Fee** | 15% - 18% | 7% - 10% | 18% - 25% |\n| **Labor Cost** | 22% - 25% | 10% - 12% | 20% - 24% |\n| **Fulfillment & Delivery** | 3% - 5% | 12% - 15% | 2% - 4% |\n| **Store Operating Margin (OPM)** | 18% - 22% | 24% - 28% | 10% - 15% |\n\n## 3. Supply Chain & Marketing Insights\n\n1. **Direct Sourcing & Roasting**: Major brands have established origin bean sourcing and automated roasting facilities. See [[Roasting Factory & Origin Sourcing]].\n2. **Product R&D**: Combined with [[Sinking Market Coffee Insights]], leverage signature milk coffee offerings to acquire and retain loyalty members.";

"demo.snippet.pkmOcrFolder" = "📷 OCR Text Extraction [Confidence: 98.9% | Source Image: Neuron_Brain_Network.png]\n\n## Neuronal Networks & Biological Brain Representation\n\nHuman memory is a complex mesh of tens of billions of neurons connected by synapses, structurally analogous to [[Value of Bi-directional Links]]:\n\n| Element | Biological Brain | ZhiYu Second Brain |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Unit** | Neuron | Atomic Card (`KnowledgePage`) |\n| **Link** | Synapse | Bi-directional Link (`[[...]]`) |\n| **Transmission** | Action Potential | Hybrid Search & Vector Cosine |\n| **Plasticity** | Neuroplasticity | 3D Graph Clustering & Emergence |\n\n> 💡 **RAG Cross-reference**: For mathematical proofs on brain representation and graph indexing, see [[Cross-Domain Note Hub Guide]].";

"demo.snippet.pkmVoiceForget" = "🎙️ Voice-to-Text Transcript [Recording Duration: 02:15 | Accuracy Confidence: 99.1%]\n\n## 1. Cognitive Psychology & Forgetting Curve Notes\n\n- **Ebbinghaus Forgetting Curve**: Memory decay is steepest within the first 24 hours (losing nearly 70% of detail). Spaced repetition must be scheduled at Day 1, Day 3, and Day 7.\n- **PKM Integration**: In [[Personal Knowledge Graph Guide]], avoid the \"Collector's Fallacy\". Ideas captured via voice notes must be refactored into [[Atomic Deconstruction of Notes]] cards within 48 hours.\n\n## 2. Action Items\n\n1. Cross-reference this transcript with [[Feynman Technique Practice]].\n2. Supplement experimental data on Active Recall in [[Progressive Summarization Analysis]].\n3. Audit unlinked orphan nodes in the active Vault.";

"demo.snippet.survey" = "# ☕ Coffee Shop Daily Operations Standard SOP Manual\n\n> This manual serves as an operational baseline guide covering morning setup, espresso dial-in calibration, extraction standards, customer complaint responses, and closing procedures. Please read alongside [[Independent Cafe Survival Guide]] and [[Third Space Design Principles]].\n\n## 1. Morning Opening Preparation (07:30 - 08:00)\n\n1. **Water & Electric Safety Inspection**: Check soft water system inlet pressure (Standard: 0.3 - 0.4 MPa). Turn on the La Marzocco dual-group espresso machine and grinder for preheating.\n2. **Hygiene & Inventory Count**: Verify stock of milk, fresh dairy, syrups, and packaging against the threshold in [[Coffee Equipment Procurement List]].\n\n## 2. Espresso Dial-in Calibration Standards\n\nA minimum of 2 quality control dial-ins must be conducted before opening daily. Test data must be logged into the daily operations journal:\n\n| Parameter Indicator | Light Roast (Ethiopia/Kenya) | Medium-Dark Roast (Blend/Colombia) | Tolerance Range |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Dose** | 19.5 g | 18.0 g | ± 0.2 g |\n| **Yield** | 42.0 g | 36.0 g | ± 1.0 g |\n| **Extraction Time** | 27 s | 25 s | ± 2 s |\n| **TDS Yield** | 9.2% - 9.8% | 9.8% - 10.5% | - |\n\n> ⚠️ **Quality Control Note**: If ambient humidity exceeds 70%, adjust the grinder to a finer step. Refer to [[Glossary: What is Coffee Roast Level]] for flavor profiles.\n\n## 3. Third Space Service & Complaint Response\n\n- Adhere to [[Third Space Design Principles]], keeping background music volume between 45-55 dB.\n- For Wi-Fi or power outlet issues, guide customers to the shared workspace area and issue drink upgrade vouchers.";
